---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ShareButtons from '../../../components/ShareButtons.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Claude Opus 5.5: Thinking You Can't Steal | Demystifying AI in 5 Minutes"
  description="Anthropic ships Claude Opus 5.5 with preserved thinking, the anti-distillation safeguard that ties reasoning chains to conversations. 40% cheaper, 85% fewer containment bypasses, always-on adaptive thinking."
  image="/og-series-ep37-claude-opus55.png"
  keywords="Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic, preserved thinking, anti-distillation, adaptive thinking, alignment, agentic coding, cache reads"
  publishedDate="2026-10-01"
  articleSection="Demystifying AI"
  articleTags={["Claude Opus 5.5", "Anthropic", "Preserved Thinking", "Anti-Distillation", "Alignment"]}
>

  <style>
    .stat-card { transition: all 0.3s ease; }
    .stat-card:hover { transform: scale(1.02); box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.1); }
    .feature-card { transition: all 0.3s ease; }
    .feature-card:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(139, 92, 246, 0.08); }
  </style>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-border">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-violet-500/[0.04] via-background to-background"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_top,rgba(139,92,246,0.06)_0%,transparent_60%)]"></div>

    <div class="relative container-main max-w-4xl pt-20 pb-10">
      <a href="/series/demystifying-ai" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-secondary hover:text-violet-400 transition-colors mb-8 font-mono">
        <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"/></svg>
        cd ~/series/demystifying-ai
      </a>

      <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-border mb-8">
        <img src="/series/ep37-claude-opus55.png" alt="Claude Opus 5.5 - Thinking You Can't Steal" class="w-full h-auto block" />
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 md:gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[10px] text-cyan font-mono bg-cyan/5 border border-cyan/20 px-2 py-1 rounded-full">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-cyan animate-pulse"></span>
          EP 37
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 text-[10px] font-mono bg-cyan/10 border border-cyan/20 text-cyan rounded-full">
          <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 7h.01M7 3h5c.512 0 1.024.195 1.414.586l7 7a2 2 0 010 2.828l-7 7a2 2 0 01-2.828 0l-7-7A1.994 1.994 0 013 12V7a4 4 0 014-4z"/></svg>
          NEW RELEASE
        </span>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">Oct 1, 2026</span>
        <span class="text-[10px] text-secondary font-mono">5 min</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground leading-tight mb-3">
        Claude Opus 5.5: Thinking You Can't Steal
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-secondary max-w-2xl mb-2">
        Anthropic ships the first 5.5 model with preserved thinking: reasoning chains cryptographically tied to conversations. 40% cheaper. 85% fewer containment bypasses. Always-on adaptive thinking.
      </p>

      <ShareButtons title="Claude Opus 5.5: Thinking You Can't Steal" url="/series/demystifying-ai/claude-opus55" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="container-main max-w-4xl py-8 md:py-10 overflow-hidden">

    <!-- TL;DR -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-4 md:p-6 mb-8 md:mb-10 max-w-3xl">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono text-violet-400 font-bold">// TL;DR</span>
      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/90 leading-relaxed mt-3 mb-0">
        Claude Opus 5.5 matches Fable 5.1 on most tasks at <strong>40% lower cost</strong>. Cache reads drop 60% to $0.20/M tokens. The real story: <strong>preserved thinking</strong> ties reasoning chains to the model and conversation, making industrial-scale distillation structurally harder. Thinking can no longer be turned off. Every API call produces a signed reasoning trace that only Anthropic's infrastructure can verify.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Stats -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mb-8 md:mb-10 max-w-3xl">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-4 text-center stat-card">
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-violet-400 mb-1">-40%</div>
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary">Net Cost</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-4 text-center stat-card">
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-violet-400 mb-1">-85%</div>
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary">Containment Bypass</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-4 text-center stat-card">
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-violet-400 mb-1">$0.20</div>
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary">Cache Reads/M</div>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-4 text-center stat-card">
        <div class="text-xl font-bold text-violet-400 mb-1">Always</div>
        <div class="text-[10px] font-mono text-secondary">Thinking On</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 1: What is Preserved Thinking -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> What Is Preserved Thinking?
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Distillation is the practice of extracting a model's capabilities at scale. Run thousands of prompts, collect the reasoning traces, and use them to train a cheaper model. Anthropic's September 2026 threat intelligence report says they have detected and disrupted this at industrial scale.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-6">
        <strong>Preserved thinking makes this structurally harder.</strong> Every thinking block gets a cryptographic signature. When you send it back in a multi-turn conversation, the API checks two things:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-5 feature-card">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="text-violet-400 text-lg">&#x1F512;</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-violet-400 font-bold">MODEL CHECK</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70">
            The thinking block was produced by the <strong>same model or an older one</strong>. Opus 5.5 reads Opus 5 thinking blocks. Opus 5 cannot read Opus 5.5 blocks. Forward compatibility, not backward.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-5 feature-card">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
            <span class="text-violet-400 text-lg">&#x1F517;</span>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono text-violet-400 font-bold">PREFIX CHECK</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70">
            The system prompt, tools, and all preceding messages are <strong>unchanged since the block was generated</strong>. Edit any prior turn? The signature breaks. The conversation must be append-only.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
        The result: even if you intercept every thinking block, the traces are cryptographically bound to a specific conversation state. Replay them in a different context and the API rejects them. Train on them and you get signatures, not reasoning.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2: API Code Example -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> What Changes in Your Code
      </h2>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        If you are already using extended thinking with Claude, the API surface barely changes. The key difference: thinking blocks are now <strong>opaque and signed</strong>. You pass them back but you cannot read or modify them.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-[#161b22] p-4 md:p-5 overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-violet-400 font-bold">MULTI-TURN WITH PRESERVED THINKING</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-[11px] font-mono leading-relaxed"><span class="text-secondary">import anthropic</span>

<span class="text-secondary">client = anthropic.Anthropic()</span>

<span class="text-violet-400 font-bold"># Turn 1: model generates preserved thinking</span>
<span class="text-secondary">response = client.messages.create(</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    model="claude-opus-5-5-20261001",</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    max_tokens=16000,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    thinking=&#123;"type": "enabled", "budget_tokens": 10000&#125;,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    messages=[&#123;"role": "user", "content": "Analyze this code..."&#125;]</span>
<span class="text-secondary">)</span>

<span class="text-violet-400 font-bold"># The thinking block is opaque — you see type + signature</span>
<span class="text-violet-400 font-bold"># You CANNOT read its content. You CAN pass it back.</span>
<span class="text-secondary">thinking_block = response.content[0]  # type: "thinking"</span>
<span class="text-secondary">text_block = response.content[1]      # type: "text"</span>

<span class="text-violet-400 font-bold"># Turn 2: pass entire content back as assistant message</span>
<span class="text-secondary">follow_up = client.messages.create(</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    model="claude-opus-5-5-20261001",</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    max_tokens=16000,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    thinking=&#123;"type": "enabled", "budget_tokens": 10000&#125;,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    messages=[</span>
<span class="text-secondary">        &#123;"role": "user", "content": "Analyze this code..."&#125;,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">        &#123;"role": "assistant", "content": response.content&#125;,</span>
<span class="text-secondary">        &#123;"role": "user", "content": "Now refactor the auth module"&#125;</span>
<span class="text-secondary">    ]</span>
<span class="text-secondary">)</span></pre>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-red-500/20 bg-red-500/[0.03] p-4 mb-6">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-red-400 font-bold">WHAT BREAKS</span>
        <div class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-[11px] text-secondary">
          <p>&#x2717; Editing or reordering previous messages → 400 error (prefix mismatch)</p>
          <p>&#x2717; Sending thinking block to a different model → 400 error (model mismatch)</p>
          <p>&#x2717; Omitting thinking block from assistant turn → model loses context, quality drops</p>
          <p>&#x2717; Setting <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">thinking: disabled</code> → no longer accepted, always-on</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3: Enforcement -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> How Enforcement Works
      </h2>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-elevated p-5 mb-6">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono text-secondary mb-3">ENFORCEMENT RULES</div>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-red-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] font-mono text-red-400 font-bold">!</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-foreground">Accounts created on/after Aug 31, 2026</span>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/60 mt-0.5">Prefix mismatch returns <strong>400 error</strong> by default. Set <code class="text-[10px] bg-elevated px-1 rounded">prefix_mismatch_behavior: "drop_block"</code> to silently drop failed blocks instead.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] font-mono text-yellow-400 font-bold">~</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-foreground">Older accounts</span>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/60 mt-0.5">Prefix check only enforced if you opt in. But Anthropic warns: <strong>later models will enforce for all accounts</strong>. Make your integration append-only now.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex-shrink-0 w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-green/20 flex items-center justify-center text-[10px] font-mono text-green font-bold">&#x2713;</span>
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold text-foreground">Model check</span>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/60 mt-0.5">Always enforced. Every account. No opt-out.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4: Cost -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> The 40% Cost Reduction
      </h2>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
        <table class="w-full text-xs">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-border">
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-3 text-secondary font-mono font-normal">Model</th>
              <th class="text-center py-3 px-3 text-secondary font-mono font-normal">Input $/M</th>
              <th class="text-center py-3 px-3 text-secondary font-mono font-normal">Output $/M</th>
              <th class="text-center py-3 px-3 text-secondary font-mono font-normal">Cache Read</th>
              <th class="text-center py-3 px-3 text-secondary font-mono font-normal">Context</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-foreground/80">
            <tr class="border-b border-border/50 bg-violet-500/[0.03]">
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 font-bold text-violet-400">Opus 5.5</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center font-bold text-violet-400">$4.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center font-bold text-violet-400">$20.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center font-bold text-violet-400">$0.20</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">200K</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/50">
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3">Opus 5</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$5.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$25.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$0.50</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">200K</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-border/50">
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3">GPT-6 Sol</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$2.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$10.00</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">N/A</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">1.05M</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3">GPT-6 Luna</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$0.10</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">$0.50</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">N/A</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center">1.05M</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
        The cache read price is the real story for agentic workloads. In coding agents and tool-use workflows, cache reads dominate the token bill. <strong>$0.20 per million cached tokens</strong> means the effective cost of long multi-turn coding sessions drops dramatically.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed">
        Context window stays at 200K. GPT-6 Sol offers 1.05M at lower raw prices, but Anthropic is betting that cache read pricing matters more than headline rates for the workflows that drive actual spend. For a 50-turn coding session with a 100K token system prompt, Opus 5.5 cache reads cost <strong>$2.00 total</strong>. On Opus 5 that was $5.00.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5: Safety -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> The Safety Numbers
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-green/20 bg-green/[0.03] p-5 feature-card">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-green font-bold block mb-3">BEHAVIORAL AUDIT</span>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70 mb-2">Nearly 2,000 adversarial scenarios.</p>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] font-mono">
              <span class="text-foreground/60">Containment bypass attempts</span>
              <span class="text-green font-bold">-85%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] font-mono">
              <span class="text-foreground/60">All bypass attempts</span>
              <span class="text-green">Low severity, self-reported</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex justify-between text-[10px] font-mono">
              <span class="text-foreground/60">Prompt injection resistance</span>
              <span class="text-green">Matches or beats Opus 5</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-violet-500/20 bg-violet-500/[0.03] p-5 feature-card">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-violet-400 font-bold block mb-3">BREAKING CHANGES</span>
          <ul class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70 space-y-2">
            <li>&#x2022; <strong>Thinking can't be disabled</strong> — always-on adaptive</li>
            <li>&#x2022; Forced tool use returns an error</li>
            <li>&#x2022; Thinking blocks tied to model + conversation</li>
            <li>&#x2022; Legacy <code class="text-[10px] bg-elevated px-1 rounded">computer_20251124</code> tool rejected</li>
            <li>&#x2022; Default effort is <code class="text-[10px] bg-elevated px-1 rounded">medium</code> (was <code class="text-[10px] bg-elevated px-1 rounded">high</code>)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Migration Checklist -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-foreground mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="text-cyan font-mono text-sm">#</span> Migration Checklist: Opus 5 → 5.5
      </h2>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-elevated p-4 md:p-5 mb-6">
        <div class="space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Make message history append-only.</strong> If your app edits or reorders previous turns, the prefix check will reject preserved thinking blocks.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Remove <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">thinking: disabled</code> from API calls.</strong> Thinking is always-on. The parameter is no longer accepted. Set <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">budget_tokens</code> low (1024) if you want minimal thinking.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Replace forced tool use.</strong> <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">tool_choice: &#123;"type": "tool", "name": "..."&#125;</code> now returns an error. Restructure your prompt to guide tool selection instead.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Pass full <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">response.content</code> as assistant turn.</strong> Both thinking and text blocks must go back. Dropping thinking blocks means the model loses its reasoning chain.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Update computer tool from <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">computer_20251124</code> to <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">computer_20260901</code>.</strong> The legacy tool spec is rejected by 5.5.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-green text-[11px]">&#x2610;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-foreground/70"><strong class="text-foreground">Test with <code class="text-[10px] bg-background px-1 rounded">prefix_mismatch_behavior: "drop_block"</code> first.</strong> Silently drops invalid thinking blocks instead of 400s. Good for debugging migration issues before going strict.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Limitations -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-10 md:mb-12">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-yellow-500/20 bg-yellow-500/[0.03] p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-yellow-400 font-bold">LIMITATIONS</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 mb-0">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-yellow-400 text-[10px] mt-0.5">&#9679;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-yellow-400">Context window still 200K.</strong> GPT-6 Sol ships with 1.05M. For workloads that need massive context, Opus 5.5 requires chunking strategies or RAG.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-yellow-400 text-[10px] mt-0.5">&#9679;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-yellow-400">Preserved thinking is opaque.</strong> You cannot inspect the reasoning chain. For debugging model behavior, you see the output but not the path. This is by design but frustrating for researchers.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-yellow-400 text-[10px] mt-0.5">&#9679;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-yellow-400">Always-on thinking adds latency.</strong> Even with budget_tokens=1024, the model still reasons before responding. Simple classification tasks that need sub-100ms responses should stay on Haiku.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="text-yellow-400 text-[10px] mt-0.5">&#9679;</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-secondary"><strong class="text-yellow-400">No vision improvements announced.</strong> Multimodal capabilities appear unchanged from Opus 5. Image and PDF understanding are stable, not enhanced.</span>
          </li>
